{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And He called.</b> Elohim, blessed be He." "<b>YHWH, YHWH.</b> He is the Cause of being who brought into existence that which did not exist, and He is the One who sustains the existence of all that exists, for no existing thing has continuance of existence apart from what flows from His existence." "<b>El.</b> Mighty regarding this — like a volitional agent — as opposed to the action that proceeds from a natural agent, which proceeds from it of necessity and not by virtue of elective power." "<b>Compassionate.</b> Toward those who deserve punishment, to lighten their punishment when they call to Him, as it says: פְּנֵי ה' בְּעוֹשֵׂי רָע וְכוּ׳ (Psalms 34:17), צָעֲקוּ וַה' שָׁמַע (Psalms 34:18). And He sees the suffering of the downtrodden, as in וְגַם רָאִיתִי אֶת הַלַּחַץ (Exodus 3:9)." "<b>And gracious.</b> He shows favor and bestows good upon those who ask, even though they are not worthy of it." "<b>Slow to anger.</b> Toward the righteous and toward the wicked, so that they may return." "<b>And abundant in kindness.</b> He inclines toward kindness in His judgment, as the Sages, of blessed memory, stated (Rosh Hashanah 17a): He passes over the first sins first — and so is this attribute." "<b>And truth.</b> And abundant in truth — He is slow to anger even in a matter that is before Him for judgment, as the Sages, of blessed memory, stated (ibid.); but one's own sin is not forgiven. And as they said: אֲשֶׁר לֹא יִשָּׂא פָנִים (Deuteronomy 10:17) — Abraham does not save Ishmael, nor Isaac save Esau; וְלֹא יִקַּח שֹׁחַד (ibid.) — a merit does not extinguish a transgression."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {7 "Index 7 in the source text includes a lemma for וֶאֱמֶת plus commentary that also addresses וְרַב אֱמֶת; the translation preserves both as Sforno wrote them."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:07.233029023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}